    "result_text": "There's only one test class and it passes. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- **`nextCustomerCode`** now takes the owner's `city` as well as `lastName`. It builds `CITY3` from the upper-cased first three letters of the city, keeps `LAST3` from the last name, and computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** sequence \u2014 one more than the count of existing owners already in that city (reusing the existing `equalsIgnoreCase` helper for case-insensitive city matching), instead of the previous global owner count.\n- The call site at `addOwner` passes `owner.getCity()` alongside the last name.\n- **Membership number** is derived from `getCustomerCode()`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `MAD-SMI-0007-M26`). I updated the Javadoc examples on both methods to reflect the new format.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting the code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.",
